                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Well it's a good first try escape room but there is a lot that needs to be fixed. So from one Unity VR developer to another, here are my tips.\n\nFirst off put a mesh collider around ALL of the object in the map... the green ball doesn't even collide with half of the objects. Secondly try VRTK... the controls are pretty bad and I can literally teleport out of the world, the only reason I can go back is because the character doesn't have gravity on his rigidbody if he has one. Thirdly (I don't even think that is a word) make it a bit more clever... looking around for cards isn't an escape the room... it's a scavenger hunt. Lastly fix the lamp... change the light or get rid of it. It doesn't even work unless I am practically touching an object with it. So please... if you ever want this game to hit it off, take my advice.",
